  "content": {
    "id": "p62-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Prove that the function $f(x)=\\dfrac{3^x}{3^{2x}+1}$ is even.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(-x)=\\dfrac{3^{-x}}{3^{-2x}+1}=\\dfrac{3^x}{1+3^{2x}}=f(x)$, so $f$ is even.",
      "worked": "For every real $x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{3^{-x}}{3^{-2x}+1}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{3^{-x}\\,3^{2x}}{(3^{-2x}+1)3^{2x}}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{3^x}{1+3^{2x}}\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nHence $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
